}
```
`rebuild()` clears `m_root` (`m_root->Clear(true)`, line 195) and rebuilds one `build_*` panel into it each call, then `Fit()`/`SetClientSize()` (223-229). Adding a webview-hosting state means either a new `build_agent_setup(wxBoxSizer&)` branched on a new dialog-local bool/state (parallel to the existing `m_agent_connected` branch inside `FlowState::Initial`, since `FlowState` itself is owned by `PrinterSetupController` and unrelated to agent connectivity) — note `rebuild()` calls `m_root->Clear(true)` which **destroys child windows**, so an embedded `wxWebView` must not be created inside `build_no_agent()`'s normal flow if it needs to survive DPI-change `rebuild()` calls (`on_dpi_changed` at line 132 also calls `rebuild()`), or it must be recreated each rebuild like every other control.

